  "post": {
    "tags": [
      "Projects"
    ],
    "summary": "Create Project",
    "description": "Creates an empty project and redirects the client to the upload service to upload files. After upload completion, the service will finalize the project automatically. Upload files with the `files` parts of the request. `fileUrls` also works for direct links to media files: an `https://` link that anyone can download and that ends in an audio or video file, not a web page. Uploading files is more robust than links.\n\nThis endpoint does not accept translation or dubbing languages — a project is created transcription-only. Once transcription completes, call `POST /v1/projects/{projectId}/recordings/{recordingId}/translate` to add translation languages, then `POST /v1/projects/{projectId}/recordings/{recordingId}/dubbing` to add dubbing languages.\n\nUpload behavior and limits:\n- 10-minute inactivity timeout per upload stream.\n- If the client connection drops, the upload is aborted and cannot resume; retry from the start.\n- Multi-hour uploads are supported as long as data keeps flowing and the connection stays open.\n\nSupported sources: files you upload and direct links to audio or video files. The file is checked after it is downloaded: if it has no audio or video stream the request is rejected with `400` and no project is created.\n\nErrors of the upload, as `{ success, statusCode, message }`:\n- `400` `The file at the URL is not an audio or video file`: the link points to a web page or another kind of file.\n- `400` `The URL could not be downloaded: the server answered <status>`: the server of the link refused, for example with `404` or `403`.\n- `400` `Invalid fileUrls entry: ...`: the link is not an `https://` URL or points to a host that is not allowed.\n- `400` `Unsupported file type. Allowed: mp4, mov, mp3, wav, m4a`: a file part of another type.\n- `400` `Invalid JSON in: <fields>`: `expectedLanguages`, `insights`, `glossary`, `safeCommunications`, `pronunciations` or `fileUrls` is not valid JSON.\n- `400` `The recording is longer than 180 minutes`: a recording may be at most 180 minutes long.\n- `400` `Maximum 50 files allowed`: a project takes at most 50 files, uploads and links together.\n- `413` a file is larger than 20 GB.\n- `502` the server of the link failed or could not be reached, or the project could not be started.\n\nCredits: the transcription of every recording uses `ceil(duration / 60)` minutes. A project whose organization has no credits left is refused with `403`.",
    "operationId": "createProject",
    "security": [
      {
        "apiKeyAuth": []
      },
      {
        "bearerAuth": []
      }
    ],
    "parameters": [
      {
        "name": "title",
        "in": "query",
        "required": false,
        "description": "Project title",
        "schema": {
          "type": "string",
          "default": "Untitled Project"
        }
      }
    ],
